= The Pandemic

A new coronavirus is spreading. By March, schools and offices close. Hospitals are overwhelmed. Everything about politics changes: campaigns, conventions, voting itself.

- @relief: Press for rapid, large-scale relief.
- @science: Defer to public-health experts.
- @voting: Fight for mail-in voting and expanded early voting.

@relief
subtitle: Government acts.
on-arrival: covid_relief = 1; pop_mod += 0.3; mod_dissent += 2; labor_dissent -= 4; stability += 2

The relief package passes with votes of both parties. Millions are spared the worst.

@science
subtitle: Credibility, unpopular lockdowns.
on-arrival: media_trust += 3; stability += 2; enthusiasm -= 1; pop_mod -= 0.1; far_right += 2

We follow public-health guidance. A noisy minority resists.

@voting
subtitle: Protects the franchise.
on-arrival: stability += 4; far_right += 3; pop_mod += 0.2

We expand access to the ballot. Opponents allege fraud, without evidence.
